  "description": "Strongly-typed Avalonia theming. Decorate a class with [Theme], install this package, and the bundled Roslyn source generator emits one {theme:PropertyName} markup extension per public property — your XAML binds theme values directly with full IntelliSense and no runtime code generation.\n\nACCENTS. {theme:AccentBrush} resolves against whichever hue the target control carries, so one accent style block serves every hue instead of a copy per accent. Callers write theme:Accent.Kind=\"Warning\"; the hue inherits, so it reaches control template parts and a container tints everything beneath it. Hues and shades are inferred from the theme's own Color Accent{Hue} and Accent{Hue}{Shade}Brush properties, so adding a hue is a theme edit and nothing else — the enum, the XAML value and the IntelliSense follow. Hues added downstream are honoured by control styles compiled before they existed.\n\nICONS. Mark a class [IconGallery] and every public string property becomes an {icons:GlyphName} extension.\n\nSTYLE CLASSES. A bundled MSBuild target generates the declarations that stop IDEs underlining Classes=\"accent\" on markup that works, keeping them in step with your ControlThemes automatically.\n\nIncludes AngelSix.ThemeEngine.SourceGen as an analyzer; a single install gives you the runtime, the generator and the build targets.",
